The mural is the valley around #link("/posts/home/")[the farm], and the lake
that covers part of it now. The hills come from the Shuttle Radar Topography
Mission (NASA and USGS, February 2000). The shore contains modified Copernicus
Sentinel data (2024), and the old river comes from Global Surface Water (EC
JRC/Google). Where one glaze ends and the next begins was chosen by eye.

The figure in the water is the writing, drawn the way a detector draws a
collision. On the first page each post is a jet and each paragraph a track; on
a post, each sentence is. Longer ones fly straighter. The dashed arrow is the
momentum that is missing.

The text is set in Spectral, the notes in Bona Nova, the formulas in New
Computer Modern, and the code in Berkeley Mono. It is written in Typst, with
comments by utterances. The rest is
#link("https://github.com/lovesegfault/blog")[in the repository].
